                "start": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Leslie Rutledge, Attorney General of Arkansas (Petitioner), according to Leslie Rutledge, Attorney General of Arkansas (Petitioner), pBMs reimburse pharmacists at rates below cost, threatening pharmacy viability."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Leslie Rutledge, Attorney General of Arkansas (Petitioner)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "699224459d84f531d4d1f9b20f538451ac65618843da57e2bd34ba0348f02e33",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-699224459d84-0000-0003",
                "ev-699224459d84-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 61,
                "start": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "ERISA does not preempt laws that implement or enforce rate regulation; Act\u202f900\u2019s enforcement mechanisms are permissible state rate regulation."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bronni",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "699224459d84f531d4d1f9b20f538451ac65618843da57e2bd34ba0348f02e33",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-699224459d84-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 61,
                "start": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bronni, requiring PBMs to reallocate part of their margin to local pharmacies will keep independent rural pharmacies open and maintain community access to pharmacy services."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner \u2013 Leslie Rutledge, Attorney General of Arkansas",
